WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.230 align:start position:0%
 
last year we set out to make the best  dungeons and dragons show on the  internet and this year we decided to  make it even better with its second  season on corridordigital.com  in making the second season we've taken  a true leap everything from cutting edge  camera tracking technology to major  motion picture visual effects workflows  all done here in corridor so today i'm  going to give you guys a little peek as  to how this has all come together  we've been following the source of this  mind player hive we need to go deeper i  have a bad feeling about this one of the  biggest improvements of this next season  is truly the storytelling we love to  play d d but not everyone likes to watch  d d which is why this show has been  edited truly like an awesome fantasy  drama you don't need to know rules of  the game and all that stuff it's really  just the best collaborative storytelling  that we can offer  i had a dream tell me on the street deep  below i saw everything i saw all of the  mind players  the story revolves around us four  adventurers you got myself and you also  have jake we have nico and we have d  nico's character nest is a warrior he's  also like a sniper type elf dude these  characters basically d in real life he's  very sinister but in a good way and we  got a bar to the group warren watts  played by none other than jake he's the  glue that keeps all of our characters  together and yeah my character is like a  giant eight foot tall goliath barbarian  i like to smash stuff sam as the dm  plays every npc in the entire game and  it makes the whole gameplay like come  alive this is not gonna feel like you're  just watching some dudes sitting around  a table it's gonna feel like you're  going on an adventure with them  [Music]  so you're probably sick of hearing about  unreal engine 5 at this point but i  can't understate how crucial it's been  to getting this show done we're  digitizing the actual real-life game  boards we're playing d d with by taking  hundreds of detailed photos of them and  then reconstructing them into these  dense super high polygon 3d models we  basically get to drop these in here and  render things out on the fly and it's  incredibly efficient i think we've  created some of the coolest scenes we've  ever done in unreal engine 5.  it's been about a year since i was in  this costume in fact i think it was last  july when we filmed the green screen  photography for season one it was a  great time season one  was ambitious pull out a green screen  and recreate the best moments at the  table playing dungeons and dragons with  our friends as an artist what i love  most in the world is finding novelty  what is like the thing that is new what  is interesting about it because it's new  we had to build a camera tracking  solution because we're dealing with  hundreds of shots and we don't want to  sit and wait while we're manually 3d  tracking all these shots for season one  i made a diy version that was uh it was  okay the problem with season one we  barely could move we maybe slide the  camera a little bit maybe move up season  two  completely different  we got early access to the htc mars  camera tracking solution and it is  incredible a setup like this allows you  to get shots that you could never get if  you were going to track your background  manually i was just whipping the camera  around i was going upside down with the  camera i was running with people across  the green screen we even get a feed  right here as we're filming so we know  what everything's going to look like as  it's shot which completely transforms  how the actors on the green screen get  to perform as well but in order to  really utilize this we're going to need  to build a huge green screen the biggest  green screen in our studio's history to  light a green screen you need a lot of  light and thankfully aperture hooked us  up with a bunch of bright leds that also  change colors that way we can light the  green screen the right color but also  light the actors and immerse them in the  world bringing the world together the  moment that made season two shooting  really stand out to me as a huge  testament to all of the hard work we've  put in over the last year and a half it  was a shot where my character was having  to walk up onto this very thin  footbridge but as ren was climbing the  virtual set we actually laid apple boxes  for him to start climbing by actually  standing up on little apple boxes and  whatnot it raises the floor plane which  allows the camera to go below it this  doesn't seem like much but it changes  everything because now by putting a  bridge in the way of the boxes i'm  actually above the camera we're getting  a more epic shot when i was trying to  get the wide shot of that very moment i  needed to look further down and there  was no more green screen so i asked to  bring a pop-up green screen and toss it  on the floor and boom the environment  appeared at my feet suddenly it's like  the freaking black hole bugs bunny thing  thrown on the ground and you have a  portal into the world we couldn't do  that last year we could do it this year  and we do it many times the best part of  it all is that at the end of the day all  i have to do is go to unreal engine hit  render on our background plates and now  suddenly we have hundreds of green  screen shots filmed on this camera  hundreds of background plates and they  all go straight to fenner for  compositing  the psychic blast comes out  30 points of damage and you're stunned  for a minute so one of the really  awesome and exciting things about the  visual effects of son of dungeon is you  know you're going from all these  different realms these different planes  every shot you're getting something new  and unique there's different monsters  there's different magic effects so it's  been a ton of fun and really you know  challenging but exciting to create these  different visual effects in season one  we had a small very indie team working  on editing and vfx for this season the  team expanded we got more editors and  more vfx artists but that also meant we  had to change the entire vfx workflow  the difference between this season and  what the team did last season with son  of a dungeon is that we are using nuke  to really speed up our workflow we're  able to template out these giant scripts  it basically has all these pre-built  effects and looks that really add a  cinematic quality to the shots with all  of the various technical upgrades to the  show it just allows sam and carmichael  to tell this story in a way that is just  a lot more freeing for them and visual  effects isn't going to be limiting that  this second season of son of a dungeon  is the biggest show that we've ever self  produced and none of it would have been  possible without the subscribers on  corridordigital.com so seriously thank  you for that if you want to see the show  head over to corridor digital.com where  we also have been documenting this  entire process in much greater detail we  would love to know what you think go to  quarterdigital.com right now the first  two episodes are already up right now  and the third one comes out in a few  days i'll be chilling in the comments  live streaming the episodes as they go  up and of course i am looking forward to  hanging out with you there  [Music]  three sheets to the wind three sheets to  the wind  i've been around the world and back  again  three sheets to the wind is where i  begin  until my time comes to an end

